[recv] {"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_0fee1f133e4096460169f9ccf390848191b1eedb0b066eb9e1","text":"Implemented the RP2040 breakout in [index.circuit.tsx](/workspace/index.circuit.tsx).\n\nWhat’s included:\n- RP2040 QFN-56, USB-C, 3.3 V LDO, external flash, 27 MHz crystal, LED, BOOT/RESET buttons, SWD/GPIO headers, decoupling, USB CC/series resistors.\n- No `routingDisabled` / `routing-disabled`.\n- No `@tsci/*` registry components.\n- JLCPCB supplier metadata added for major parts.\n- Output generated at [dist/index/circuit.json](/workspace/dist/index/circuit.json).\n\nVerification:\n- `npm run typecheck`: passed\n- `tsci check netlist index.circuit.tsx`: passed, 0 errors / 0 warnings\n- `tsci check placement index.circuit.tsx`: passed, 0 errors / 0 warnings\n- `tsci build index.circuit.tsx`: wrote circuit JSON, but reported routing/DRC errors from the autorouter on this dense breakout.\n\n**TSCircuit Developer Feedback**\n- Confusing/surprising: built-in USB-C semantic pins changed when a KiCad footprint was added, requiring manual alias mapping.\n- Most time wasted: autorouting diagnostics and router behavior, especially with dense QFN-to-header traces.\n- Helpful improvements: clearer docs for USB-C `standard` plus explicit footprint pin-label behavior, and examples for JLCPCB/KiCad footprint alias mapping.\n- Friction points: `tsci init` attempted GitHub skill setup and hit rate limits; footprint strings like `smd3225` are easy to guess but invalid; supplier footprint mismatch warnings are noisy for generic passives.\n- Time-wasting CLI command: `tsci check routing-difficulty index.circuit.tsx` hung and had to be killed. It should have a default timeout, progress output, and a concise failure summary. The default `tsci build` capacity autorouter also hung/failed on routing; exposing router progress and suggested layout changes would make it much easier to act on.","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null},"threadId":"019df7b6-32af-7c43-8389-041c17b22a18","turnId":"019df7b6-32bb-7ba2-9bef-229ce349c329"}}
